[02:59.98]Q2. What does the man say the government of Winopia is probably undergoing?
[03:18.94]Q3. According to the man, how does one get a career in foreign relations?
[03:37.62]Q4. What do the speakers mainly discuss by the end of the conversation?
[03:57.20]M: It's getting late and we're both displaying signs of weariness.
[04:01.28]M: I think we should call it a day and meet again tomorrow morning.
[04:04.10]W: Oh, come on, Jeff.
[04:05.48]W: We are so close!
[04:07.00]W: Don't you think we are almost done?
[04:08.94]W: Let's do two more hours, please.
[04:11.90]M: One hour, then I'm going home.
[04:14.40]W: OK, fine.
[04:15.12]W: I think we are making good progress, and that with a few more amendments, we will be all done.
[04:21.68]M: I'm sure looking forward to it.
[04:23.64]M: I'm so tired of this project.
[04:25.78]M: Don't get me wrong.
[04:27.10]M: It's a great professional opportunity for me and a milestone for the company, but it's just been so long.
[04:33.28]W: Yeah.
[04:34.54]W: Two months working on nothing but the same contract is a little tough.
[04:38.90]W: Nevertheless, I think that with a bit of luck, we'll be done by next week.
[04:43.66]M: Ha, you must be delusional.
[04:46.12]W: You don't think so?
[04:47.48]M: No chance.
[04:49.16]M: Sections 4, 5, 8 and 9 still have to be aligned to the new framework.
[04:54.24]M: Then we need to proofread the whole thing and make sure all selling points are watertight.
[04:59.76]W: But that will all take no more than a couple of days.
[05:02.52]M: I wasn't finished.
[05:04.52]M: When we are done with it and send it upstairs, what do you think will happen?
[05:08.82]W: What?
[05:09.44]M: They'll argue about it for like a month.
[05:12.18]M: There's always going to be the odd board member who intervenes and demands rectifications be made.
[05:17.52]M: They might think that being helpful, but in reality that being obstructive and hampering progress.
[05:22.22]W: Oh, Jeff, you're too preoccupied and cynical.
[05:26.32]W: It won't be anywhere as bad as that.
[05:28.18]W: You'll see, the entire managerial hierarchy wants to see this project implemented as soon as possible, and the board, too, is virtually unanimous in its support.
[05:38.98]W: Go on then, let's stop there and meet up again same time tomorrow.
